      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-297613",
      ":question/problem": "For a wildlife study, Nora recorded whether deer were spotted during morning and evening hikes over $10$ weekends. Her results are shown in the table below.\n\n|  | Deer spotted | No deer spotted | Total |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Morning hikes | $11$ | $9$ | $20$ |\n| Evening hikes | $6$ | $14$ | $20$ |\n| **Total** | **$17$** | **$23$** | **$40$** |\n\nIf one of the hikes on which no deer were spotted is selected at random, what is the probability the hike was in the evening?"
